{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q421994","formula":"C₈H₁₇N","hill":"C8H17N","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":8.0,"H":17.0,"N":1.0},"names":{"en":"Coniine","ru":"Кониин","uk":"Коніїн"},"descriptions":{"en":"Coniine is a poisonous chemical compound, an alkaloid present in and isolable from poison hemlock (Conium maculatum), where its presence has been a source of significant economic, medical, and historico-cultural interest; coniine is also produced by the yellow pitcher plant (Sarracenia flava), and fool's parsley (Aethusa cynapium). Its ingestion and extended exposure are toxic to humans and all classes of livestock; its mechanism of poisoning involves disruption of the central nervous system, with death caused by respiratory paralysis.","ru":"Кониин — сильный яд нервно-паралитического действия. Химическая формула — C8H17N, основной алкалоид и ядовитое начало болиголова пятнистого (Conium maculatum).","uk":"Конії́н (англ. Coniine) — сильна отрута нервово-паралітичної дії. Хімічна формула — C8H17N, основний алкалоїд (групи піперидину) і отруйна складова болиголова плямистого (Conium maculatum)."},"fame":29,"pubchemCid":441072,"mass":127.23,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCC[C@H]1CCCCN1","inchikey":"NDNUANOUGZGEPO-QMMMGPOBSA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-propylpiperidine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"441072","atoms":26,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.856,"y":1.318,"z":-0.178,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.071,"y":0.277,"z":0.282,"el":"C"},{"x":0.354,"y":-1.101,"z":-0.243,"el":"C"},{"x":1.792,"y":-1.425,"z":0.156,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.482,"y":0.619,"z":-0.194,"el":"C"},{"x":2.728,"y":-0.293,"z":-0.253,"el":"C"},{"x":2.226,"y":1.054,"z":0.261,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.501,"y":-0.387,"z":0.332,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.901,"y":-0.061,"z":-0.162,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.067,"y":0.261,"z":1.38,"el":"H"